she was going to the dentist?
她要去看牙医？

4
00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:27,320
I crossed the street to avoid meeting him but he saw me and came running towards me.
我穿过马路以便避开他，但他看见了我，朝我跑过来。

5
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:34,160
It was no use pretending that I had not seen him, so I waved to him.
装作没看见他已经没用了，所以我向他挥手。

6
00:00:34,790 --> 00:00:38,500
I never enjoy meeting Nigel Dykes.
我从来不喜欢遇见奈杰尔·戴克斯。

7
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:41,470
He never has anything to do.
他从来无事可做。

8
00:00:42,670 --> 00:00:48,420
No matter how busy you are, he always insists on coming with you.
不管你多忙，他总是坚持要跟你一起去。

9
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:55,010
I had to think of a way of preventing him from following me around all morning.
我得想个办法，不让他整个上午都跟着我。

10
00:00:57,350 --> 00:01:01,680
'Hello, Nigel,' I said 'Fancy meeting you here!'
“你好，奈杰尔，”我说，“想不到在这儿遇见你！”

11
00:01:02,860 --> 00:01:05,470
'Hi, Elizabeth,' Nigel answered.
“你好，伊丽莎白，”奈杰尔回答说。

12
00:01:06,460 --> 00:01:12,050
'I was just wondering how to spend the morning--until I saw you.
“我正在发愁这个上午怎么打发——直到看见你。

13
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:16,350
You're not busy doing anything, are you?'
你不忙吧，是吗？”

14
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:22,430
'No, not at all,' I answered. 'I'm going to...'
“不，一点也不忙，”我回答说，“我正要去……”

15
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:26,340
'Would you mind my coming with you?'
“我跟你一起去你不介意吧？”

16
00:01:26,610 --> 00:01:30,260
he asked, before I had finished speaking.
他没等我说完就问。

17
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:36,350
'Not at all,' I lied, 'but I'm going to the dentist.'
“一点也不，”我撒谎说，“不过我要去看牙医。”

18
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:40,610
'Then I'll come with you,' he answered.
“那我跟你一起去，”他回答说。

19
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:45,070
'There's always plenty to read in the waiting room!'
“候诊室里总是有很多东西可看！”
